<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rwenzori Mountains</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ruwenzori</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Rwenzori Mountains are a range on the border between Uganda and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/democratic-republic-of-the-congo">Democratic Republic of the Congo</a>, rising to 5,109 metres at Margherita Peak on Mount Stanley. They carry some of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>'s last equatorial glaciers and are often identified with Ptolemy's Mountains of the Moon. The fertile lands at their foot formed the Kingdom of Toro.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rwenzori-mountains.jpg" alt="Rwenzori Mountains" width="320" height="211" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nick06 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1172_ruwenzori.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Around 1830 Prince Kaboyo Olimi I, a son of the omukama of the Kingdom of Bunyoro, rebelled and set up an independent kingdom in the fertile lands around the <b>Rwenzori Mountains</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-toro">Kingdom of Toro</a></li></ul></section>
